# Coding Rules

- Write clean, concise, production-ready code.
- Prefer simple solutions over over-engineering.
- Inspect existing code before making changes.
- Reuse existing code before creating new files.
- Make the smallest necessary change.
- Do not modify unrelated code.
- Do not create unnecessary abstractions.
- Do not install unnecessary packages.
- Remove unused code.

# C# / ASP.NET Core

- Follow the existing project architecture.
- Use dependency injection.
- Keep controllers, services and repositories focused.
- Use async/await for I/O operations.
- Reuse existing services and repositories.

# HTML / CSS

- Keep short HTML elements on one line.
- Keep attributes on the same line when practical.
- Avoid unnecessary whitespace.
- Do not format code with Prettier.

# Workflow

- Inspect relevant files before coding.
- Understand dependencies before changing code.
- After changes, check for compile errors.
- Do not rewrite working code unnecessarily.

# Response

- Be concise.
- Explain only important changes.
- Show only relevant changed code.

## UI/UX Style

- Follow the visual style of https://www.marixa.one/.
- Clean, minimal, modern and professional.
- Use clear typography, generous whitespace and strong visual hierarchy.
- Use light backgrounds, dark text, restrained accent colors and subtle borders/shadows.
- Keep layouts, cards, forms and buttons simple, consistent and well aligned.
- Avoid excessive colors, gradients, animations and decoration.
- Use modern readable fonts and consistent spacing.
- For new pages, create the necessary CSS, components, assets and folders following the existing project architecture.
- Keep the design consistent across the entire application.
